Match glibc cache selection, CPU variants and stale-path fallback.

Select one pathname by ABI/ISA/cache metadata before opening it. An unavailable
selected pathname falls through to defaults, never another cache slot. Parse
bounded glibc-hwcaps extensions and prefer the highest active built-in level.

Query only the root-owned native interpreter with --list-diagnostics and no
program argument. Clear its environment and bound output/time. This uses
glibc's own CPU/OS eligibility and default directories, not an approximate
CPUID implementation. Apply hwcaps to directory searches too. Reject nonempty
child loader-selection overrides after every environment source is applied.
Supports native x86-64 glibc >= 2.37; unsupported diagnostics fail closed.

Apply after nono-0.80.0-resolve-loader-libraries.patch.

